      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ἡμεῖς τὸ βοηθούμενον, „σὺ ὁ βοηθός“, „ὁ ἰατρός“, „ὁ σωτήρ“, „τὸ τεῖχος“, ἡ ζωή, „ἡ ἐλπίς“, „ἡ καταφυγή“, ἡ χαρά, ἡ προσδοκία.",
          "english_quote": "We are those who receive help; you are the helper, the physician, the Savior, the wall, the life, the hope, the refuge, the joy, the expectation, and the rest.",
          "issue": "The words survive, but the selected edition’s six separately marked quotations have been absorbed into an unmarked enumeration. The outer quotation marks around the entire prayer do not preserve the distinction between these quoted expressions and the intervening unquoted attributes.",
          "suggested_revision": "Restore inner quotation boundaries around “you are the helper,” “the physician,” “the Savior,” “the wall,” “the hope,” and “the refuge,” using single quotation marks inside the quoted prayer. Keep the other attributes outside those inner quotations. This is preservation of the supplied editorial presentation, not a textual correction.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἡ ἀνάπαυσις",
          "english_quote": "and the rest.",
          "issue": "In an enumeration, “and the rest” ordinarily means the unspecified remainder of the list. Here ἀνάπαυσις names rest or repose as another divine attribute; it is not a catch-all expression. The English introduces an avoidable ambiguity absent from this Greek noun.",
          "suggested_revision": "Replace “and the rest” with “and rest” or “and repose,” making this a distinct predicate rather than an unspecified remainder. The revised wording requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "3.73",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": true,
        "no_added_claims": true,
