      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "Μέλλων ἐπὶ τὴν Τύρον ὁρμᾶν μεθ’ ἡμέρας ἑπτὰ βούλομαι ἐξ αὐτῆς ὑμᾶς ἀπελθόντας",
          "english_quote": "The feminine pronoun occurs twice without an explicit feminine antecedent in this excerpt.",
          "issue": "The disclosure is overbroad: Tyre is an explicit feminine antecedent candidate immediately before the first ἐξ αὐτῆς. What is absent is an explicit antecedent naming the current city required by the chosen spatial interpretation. The lexical note also calls Tyre “subsequently named,” although it has already been named here. Furthermore, the ensuing journey to Tyre is compatible with both the contextual spatial reading and the idiomatic temporal reading “at once”; it does not by itself establish their relative likelihood. The spatial main rendering remains a defensible contextual choice, but its supporting disclosure needs correction.",
          "suggested_revision": "Revise both notes to explain that Tyre precedes the first occurrence, while the main translation instead supplies an implicit reference to the current city. Explicitly retain the idiomatic alternative “at once” for both occurrences and explain that the ensuing journey is compatible with either interpretation. Remove the inaccurate word-order statement and qualify the comparative-likelihood claim. No source correction or print verification is required; the revised disclosure must undergo fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
